  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Merits and demerits"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Merits: no inductors, so it is simple, cheap and compact; it gives a good sine wave at audio and low frequencies (a few Hz to about 100 kHz). Demerits: tuning is awkward, because all three R or all three C must be changed together; it needs a high gain of 29; and the amplitude is less stable, so it is used mainly at fixed audio frequencies."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Merits: no coils, simple, good at audio frequencies"
    },
    {
     "en": "Demerits: hard to tune, needs A ≥ 29"
    },
    {
     "en": "Used for fixed low frequencies"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The RC phase-shift oscillator is simple and good for audio, but it is hard to tune because three components must change together.",
    "kn": "RC ಹಂತ-ಸ್ಥಾನಾಂತರ ಆಂದೋಲಕ ಸರಳ ಮತ್ತು ಶ್ರವ್ಯ ಆವೃತ್ತಿಗೆ ಉತ್ತಮ, ಆದರೆ ಮೂರು ಘಟಕಗಳನ್ನು ಒಟ್ಟಿಗೆ ಬದಲಿಸಬೇಕಾದ್ದರಿಂದ ಟ್ಯೂನ್ ಮಾಡುವುದು ಕಷ್ಟ."
   }
